<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Australis shares rise on ACCC approval.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Australis shares rise on ACCC approval.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-10-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Australis Media Ltd rose more than 30 percent after the Australian Competition and Consumer Competition (ACCC) approved the company's satellite deal with fellow pay TV group Optus Vision.</p>
<p>At 2.00 p.m. (0400 GMT), Australis was six cents or 31.58 percent higher at 25 cents with nearly three million shares traded.  </p>
<p>ACCC said earlier it would not oppose the DTH satellite joint venture as the two satellite pay TV providers would compete in terms of pricing, marketing and programme content.</p>
<p>The satellite deal with Optus Vision was seen a key part of Australis recapitalisation plan, which was also approved by the ACCC.</p>
<p>-- Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373 1800</p>
</text>
